EAS COJO dual-mode V5
=====================

One codebase supports two runs via EAS_RUN_MODE.

1) Primary run
--------------
Command:
  EAS_RUN_MODE=primary bash run_EAS_COJO_dualmode_V5.sh

Definition:
  - EAS evidence only (BBJ/TWB/TPMI)
  - source-specific 1000G EAS clumping
  - direct KoGES-exact rescue is still identified/audited, but is NOT inserted
    into the primary condition set
  - at least one 1000G EAS clump-defined signal is required for a target to be
    ready
  - Step1 (shared with V4):
      COJO/EAS-only/step1
  - 1000G clumping panel:
      COJO/1000G_LD_panel_indel
  - default Step2 directory:
      COJO/EAS-only/ancestry_clumped_1000G_V5_EAS_primary_clumponly
  - default MA directory:
      COJO/EAS-only/GCTA_ma_V5_EAS_primary_clumponly
  - default GCTA directory:
      COJO/EAS-only/GCTA_conditional_V5_EAS_primary_clumponly
  - default logs / KoGES LD reference:
      COJO/EAS-only/logs_V5_EAS_primary_clumponly
      COJO/EAS-only/KoGES_COJO_LD_reference_V5_EAS_primary_clumponly

2) Rescue-augmented sensitivity run
-----------------------------------
Command:
  EAS_RUN_MODE=sensitivity bash run_EAS_COJO_dualmode_V5.sh

Definition:
  - same 1000G EAS clump-defined condition set
  - plus 1000G-unmatched external EAS GWS variants that resolve exactly to one
    KoGES variant
  - same-source rescue-rescue and rescue-clump redundancy can be collapsed by
    KoGES r^2 >= 0.9; a 1000G clump representative outranks a rescue SNP
  - rescue-only targets are allowed as sensitivity evidence
  - default Step2 directory:
      COJO/EAS-only/ancestry_clumped_1000G_V5_EAS_sensitivity_rescue
  - default MA directory:
      COJO/EAS-only/GCTA_ma_V5_EAS_sensitivity_rescue
  - default GCTA directory:
      COJO/EAS-only/GCTA_conditional_V5_EAS_sensitivity_rescue
  - default logs / KoGES LD reference:
      COJO/EAS-only/logs_V5_EAS_sensitivity_rescue
      COJO/EAS-only/KoGES_COJO_LD_reference_V5_EAS_sensitivity_rescue

Step3c final-verdict safeguards
-------------------------------
- independent and not-conditionally-GWS verdicts require
  condition_set_effectively_complete_GCTA == TRUE.
- high-LD is kept as a separate evidence category and does not require an
  effectively complete conditional model; it requires the Step3b high-LD logic
  based on directly measured lead-condition KoGES LD in a non-finite/collinear
  COJO setting.
- paper-facing output includes:
    condition_set_effectively_complete_GCTA
    GCTA_run_status
    EAS_run_mode
    primary_condition_set

Recommended order if both runs will be performed
------------------------------------------------
  EAS_RUN_MODE=primary     bash run_EAS_COJO_dualmode_V5.sh
  EAS_RUN_MODE=sensitivity bash run_EAS_COJO_dualmode_V5.sh
  Rscript --vanilla step3d.compare_EAS_dualmode_V5.R

The two runs use separate output directories automatically and therefore do not
reuse Step2/Step3 products across modes.

Dual-mode comparison (Step3d)
-----------------------------
Step3d uses the primary integrated table as the master denominator and joins
the rescue-augmented sensitivity result by target_id.  It verifies that every
primary-ready target is sensitivity-ready and that the primary 1000G-clump
condition set is a subset of the corresponding sensitivity condition set.

The comparison status distinguishes:
  - robust_independent_after_rescue_sensitivity
  - independence_sensitive_to_direct_KoGES_rescue
  - sensitivity_unassessable
  - primary_not_independent
  - sensitivity_only_rescue_target_no_primary_claim

Only the first category supports a robust additional-independent-association
claim.  A sensitivity-only rescue target is retained as sensitivity evidence,
not as a primary result.

Default comparison output:
  COJO/EAS-only/GCTA_conditional_V5_EAS_dualmode_comparison.tsv

